From: rhodep port
Subject: [PATCH] DIAGNOSTIC: btqca: make the TLV segment size settable

Not for upstream. The QCA firmware download fails with -110 after a warm
reset while the short EDL version command on the same link still works,
and forcing the link down to 115200 does not help, so the length of the
transfer is the remaining suspect rather than the link speed. This makes
the segment size a module parameter so the two can be told apart without
a rebuild per data point.

--- a/drivers/bluetooth/btqca.c	2026-08-28 16:37:22.697509001 +0000
+++ b/drivers/bluetooth/btqca.c	2026-08-28 16:37:22.707509001 +0000
@@ -13,6 +13,11 @@
 
 #include "btqca.h"
 
+static unsigned int tlv_seg_size = MAX_SIZE_PER_TLV_SEGMENT;
+module_param(tlv_seg_size, uint, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(tlv_seg_size,
+		 "DIAGNOSTIC: bytes per TLV segment during firmware download");
+
 int qca_read_soc_version(struct hci_dev *hdev, struct qca_btsoc_version *ver,
 			 enum qca_btsoc_type soc_type)
 {
@@ -621,7 +626,12 @@
 	segment = data;
 	remain = size;
 	while (remain > 0) {
-		int segsize = min(MAX_SIZE_PER_TLV_SEGMENT, remain);
+		unsigned int lim = tlv_seg_size;
+		int segsize;
+
+		if (lim == 0 || lim > MAX_SIZE_PER_TLV_SEGMENT)
+			lim = MAX_SIZE_PER_TLV_SEGMENT;
+		segsize = min_t(int, lim, remain);
 
 		bt_dev_dbg(hdev, "Send segment %d, size %d", i++, segsize);
 
